WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.770
Perpetuate existence.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.910
Wh-What's this?

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.260
She has forced Naenia
to take a bodily form!

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.390
I've thought about this ever so long.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:42.060
How could I end this perpetual nightmare?

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.650
How could I lay hands
upon this incorporeal thing?

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.070
At last.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.030
Now, even I could slay you.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.490
There is something I wish you to know.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.410
My father told me,

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.660
"Those born into the nobility
must protect their fief's people.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.210
The d'Apchier family
takes pride in doing that."

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:14.010
Therefore, no matter what they do to me
or how much I wish to kill them,

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.550
I could never hate the people
of the d'Apchier fiefdom!

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.050
I love them!

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.180
It is the sworn duty
of those born a d'Apchier.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.430
But you, I cannot forgive,

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.980
for you took my one, my only,

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.520
and laid hands upon him.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.110
You defiled Jean-Jacques's true name.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.740
I shall <i>never</i> forgive that.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.660
As I told you,

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:43.160
I am a terribly jealous woman.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.250
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.420
What is that sound?!

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.550
W-We have a problem, Captain!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:26.220
I'm picking up tremendous
waves of energy from that castle.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.730
I believe the engine
may have been activated!

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.520
To the castle!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.860
Astolfo, wait!

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.860
This is <i>not</i> good.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.240
Something is going on in there.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:45.660
Vanitas!

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.410
Are you all right?! Vanitas!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.250
Mademoiselle Chloé?! Naenia?!

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:01.420
You're harder to kill than I thought.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.640
Does it hurt? Are you in pain?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.270
Can you feel my rage?

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.980
Don't... do this.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.360
Vanitas.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.940
Do not provoke Naenia anymore than this.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.130
Oh, the pain!

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.430
It hurts so bad!

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:51.970
It hurts!

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:01.480
Chloé! Release her from bodily form!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.820
Don't make her remember who she really is!

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.160
You won't be able to kill it!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:26.220
B-Brother... what was that?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.840
Calm yourself, Luca.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:35.680
We tried so very hard to destroy her body.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.730
It seems there were still
some remains scattered about.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:43.570
Isn't that right, my queen?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.920
That oppressive force,
it turns my stomach!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.260
What is happening?

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:14.430
My body won't stop trembling.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:19.560
It will not let me defy
the presence before me.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:34.660
Mademoiselle Chloé!

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.410
No! She'll come after you, too!

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.460
Vanitas, what is happening?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.750
That thing, Naenia, what is it?

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:48.130
That is Naenia, Death's Keeper.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:59.940
It is the malnomen of Queen Faustina,
the first vampire of the crimson moon.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.400
Her Majesty, the Queen?

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:08.650
This is bad!

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.660
Her malady was forcibly manifested!
She'll spiral out of control!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.630
Jean-Jacques!

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.640
Chloé?

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.760
C-Captain! We're floating in thin air!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.970
The whole place is floating!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.760
The engine halted!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.470
Naenia will be disembodied once more!

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:32.280
I almost forgot.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.990
I must seek out more names.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.170
Vanitas!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.850
You will fail.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.980
You will never reach him.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.770
No one can save him.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.770
All is lost.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:12.280
So why do you keep reaching out?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:15.570
Hurry up and join us.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.960
What the devil was that?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.750
What happened?

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.170
Where are we?

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.960
Our village is gone?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.090
It's so cold.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.380
Look!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.300
The villagers of Saugues, no doubt.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.720
Vanitas.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.720
Curse that wretched Naenia.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.640
Why couldn't she just quietly disappear?

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.230
She truly is rotten to the core.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.770
Listen to me, Noé.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:51.360
Chloé d'Apchier's malnomen
creates a space that protects her.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:55.030
And as it spirals out of control,
it corrupts an ever wider area,

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:58.280
drawing in every living thing in its path.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:02.370
It will devour everyone in Gévaudan
if we don't do something.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.210
You knew?!

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:13.800
You should have filled me
in if you knew about all this!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:14.630
What?!

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:18.130
And not just about Chloé!
About Naenia, too!

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:20.890
I wasn't sure about
her true identity till now!

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.260
And I don't like willy-nilly conjecture!

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.350
Got a problem with that?!

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.560
I do!

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.100
If you'd told me, things would've
turned out different!

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.730
Or not. There's no way to know for sure!

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.690
But maybe we could have done something!

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:36.240
--I could've--

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.150
--You wouldn't have believed me!
--I could've--

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.740
You vampires never listen to humans!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:47.080
Do you even realize how many times
I've nearly been slain by your kind?!

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.500
And we're talking about
your queen this time!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.210
Yes, but I--

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.590
Did you already forget how
Lord Ruthven nearly did me in?!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.510
You <i>complete</i> moron!

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.430
I believe you!

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:09.940
Ouch! Stop it!

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.190
You make me sick!

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.310
What's that for?

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:13.560
You really make me sick!

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.190
That hurts.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.490
So? What now?

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.200
Oh, um...

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.580
You haven't given up on
Chloé d'Apchier, have you?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.750
Of course not!

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.840
Wolves?!

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.720
I'll let Vanitas handle this while I...

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.470
No, I better not.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.600
These are no ordinary wolves.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.350
There's no time!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:55.980
What shall I do?!

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.780
Let's have at them, Durendal.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.740
I thought it was you two.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:10.000
I always knew we'd meet again.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.460
I am ever grateful
for God's guiding light.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.630
Thank you, O Lord!

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.640
Roland!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.770
Orcas?!

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.520
Forgive me, but those
are Chasseur transports.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:41.990
Things might go south
if they were to spot you.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:44.150
It was quite a shock.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:47.780
We were suddenly caught in
a blizzard on the way to Saugues.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.500
Then mountains began to crumble,
and wolves attacked.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:56.080
The Beast of Gévaudan
must be behind all this.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:59.630
Don't tell me Roland is here
to kill the Beast, too?

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.010
Actually...

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:03.800
So what's the plan?

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.180
If you two are here,

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:11.060
there must be a curse-bearing
vampire at the center of all this.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.770
What can I do to affect
a more peaceful resolution?

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:22.780
Roland!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.150
That fool!

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:27.530
He vanished, leaving us in the lurch.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:31.490
You wish to help us? But why?

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.160
How can you say that?

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:37.580
I thought it was obvious
that I'm quite fond of you two.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:43.920
Me, too! I'm quite fond... of you!

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.220
I thank you both!

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.380
Don't drag me into this!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:52.100
Don't let the people
of Gévaudan die, Roland.

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:58.270
Fulfilling her duty as a d'Apchier
gives meaning to Chloé's life.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:03.860
So if she were to lose control and
kill even one denizen of this region,

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.490
there would be no saving her.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:11.910
And even if we did save her,
there would be no salvation for her soul.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:14.120
Can you do that?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.040
Leave it to me.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:21.670
However, I am here as
a paladin of the Chasseurs.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.840
If the situation gets much worse,

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.970
I will not hesitate to
start beheading vampires.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.100
Don't force me to slay the Beast.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.350
Now that that's settled,
it's time to get to work!

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:42.900
You two take care of what only you can do!

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.160
Hauteclaire.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:54.080
You will break it again if you
keep handling it so roughly.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.580
What?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.210
You always did fight in
a most uncivilized manner.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.630
Hold your tongue!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.960
Where were you?!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:06.960
Yes, about that, Olivier.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.470
May I ask you to do me a favor?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.010
No, you cannot.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.140
In that case,

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:15.850
I need, let's see... I'd say
about 30 minutes of your time.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.640
We are going on a rescue mission!

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.100
I already said no!

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.690
But you don't agree
with the order, do you?

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:23.610
Huh?

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:28.900
The order that said, "Slay every
vampire you encounter in Gévaudan."

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.700
We're not at war here.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:36.330
Killing innocent vampires will only
lead to problems that are far worse.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:41.290
It's almost as if the Church
is trying to cover up something.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.420
That doesn't sit well with me.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:54.090
So I'd like to speak with the
curse-bearer up there without killing her.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:57.890
Speak with a curse-bearer?
Don't tell me...!

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:01.100
Those two are at it again?!

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.940
Well, what do we have here?

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.610
Georges! Maria!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.190
Olivier and I will destroy
this abomination!

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.400
The rescue effort is your top priority!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.200
I don't want a single casualty!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.530
Yes, sir!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:19.240
It's been ages since
I fought by your side.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.660
Then let's be quick about it!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.430
Where am I?

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.560
Who am I?

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:48.070
You are but a puppet and nothing more.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.480
You need but be a tool.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.780
A vessel needs not a will of its own.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:55.990
Think not.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.990
Have not wants nor wishes.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:03.160
Fail in this, and we
shall claim your head.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.960
I am a puppet.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.340
Nothing but a tool.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.300
Little girl, are you all alone?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.010
Are you all right?

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:28.940
Yes, we've decided to
raise the child ourselves.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:31.190
It is a pleasure to meet you, Jeanne.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:33.030
I am Ruthven.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:37.530
Henceforth, I want you to see and
learn all you can under my tutelage.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.160
You must learn about this world.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:48.000
Mother. Father. I'll see you again soon!

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:02.100
Your mother and father
betrayed the vampires.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:06.350
Their betrayal led to the death
of our brethren in untold numbers.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.150
Children must atone
for their parent's sins.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.230
No longer are you a vampire.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:14.990
You are a tool, a bourreau.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:19.660
Think not.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.790
Have not wants nor wishes.

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:26.160
Fail in this, and...

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.960
So that's why.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.830
I didn't do what I was told.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:35.510
But they took my parents'
heads instead of mine.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:40.970
I am a bourreau.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:45.020
I am but a tool.
I need only follow my orders.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:50.810
So you're... the Hellfire Witch?

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:54.360
Go on, quickly now.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:59.450
Use your fangs, your talons,
your flames, and...

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.570
Jeanne.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.540
Think not.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.630
Have not wants nor wishes.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.550
Fail in this, and...

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.220
No. Please.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:22.050
I will slay her. Please!

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.020
Jeanne?

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.390
Jeanne!

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.410
Lord Ruthven.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:30.410
Jeanne, do not forget
the oath you just swore.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:39.380
You shall now enter a long slumber.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:44.970
You shall sleep until the war ends
and all can live in peace.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:48.100
Use this time to heal both body and mind.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:56.610
Yes, I had forgotten.

00:20:56.610 --> 00:21:00.190
For that dream was so very long.

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:02.990
It made me forget that I was a puppet,

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:06.910
and that I must have no will of my own.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:13.460
I must kill Chloé this time.
I must not fail.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:16.420
Chloé d'Apchier is not the Beast.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.710
You've seen it with your own eyes.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.250
That doesn't matter.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:25.380
Lord Ruthven ordered me to put
an end to the trouble in Gévaudan.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:28.220
But he never told you to kill her.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:32.520
Do you realize how many lives
the Beast of Gévaudan has claimed?

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:35.230
I have no choice but to slay it.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.900
And Chloé is a curse-bearer.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:44.240
Bourreaus must execute
curse-bearers that have lost control.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.200
It's too late now.

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.120
She's beyond help.

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.790
That's why I must--

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.790
It's not too late!

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:05.010
"Hands upon a Nightmare"

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:41.500
"Just the Two of Us"
